==================================================
7. HISTORICAL DATA VS CURRENT STATE
==================================================

Do NOT throw away historical player statistics after a transfer.

Historical data is still valuable for modelling underlying ability.

But separate:

HISTORICAL PERFORMANCE

from

CURRENT CLUB

from

CURRENT ROLE

from

CURRENT FIXTURES

from

CURRENT AVAILABILITY.

A transferred player's historical performance may remain in the model.

His previous club must NOT determine his current fixtures.

His previous club must NOT determine his current starting probability
unless explicitly justified by transferable evidence.

